      en: "Huddinge is a municipality south of Stockholm, known for its blend of urban development and natural landscapes. The area was originally farmland but transformed after the arrival of the railway in the late 1800s. Modern Huddinge is defined by its educational and medical institutions, including the Karolinska University Hospital campus and Södertörn University. The municipality has a rich Viking history, with burial mounds and runestones scattered throughout. Its cultural scene includes the Huddinge Museum and the annual Huddinge Festival. With 45% forest cover, Huddinge is a green suburb that attracts families and academics alike.",
